# D14 — GeneralizedWfstBuilder configuration flow.
# Depicts: the fluent builder chain, the runtime-selectable OperationSet, and the lazy product graph.
direction: right

title: |md
  # D14 · GeneralizedWfstBuilder configuration flow
| { near: top-center }

new: "new(&dict)" { style.fill: "#D6EAF8"; style.stroke: "#34495E" }
cfg: ".query(q)\n.max_distance(k)" { style.fill: "#D6EAF8"; style.stroke: "#34495E" }

ops: "choose an OperationSet" {
  style.fill: "#EAECEE"; style.stroke: "#34495E"
  std: "with_standard_ops()" { style.fill: "#FCF3CF" }
  tr:  "with_transposition()" { style.fill: "#FCF3CF" }
  ms:  "with_merge_split()" { style.fill: "#FCF3CF" }
  ph:  "with_phonetic_digraphs()" { style.fill: "#D5F5E3" }
  custom: "with_operations(set)" { style.fill: "#FCF3CF" }
}

build: "build()\n→ Result<GeneralizedWfst<D>, String>" { style.fill: "#D6EAF8"; style.stroke: "#34495E" }
wfst: "GeneralizedWfst<D>\nexact-cost scale, limits, and transactional lazy product" {
  style.fill: "#D6EAF8"; style.stroke: "#34495E"
}

new -> cfg -> ops -> build -> wfst { style.stroke: "#34495E" }

product: |md
  **Lazy product graph:** `GeneralizedWfst` registers product states
  `(dict_node, query_byte_offset, accumulated_cost)` and continuation states for multi-symbol
  operations such as `ph : f / 0.15`. `StateSource::compute_state` returns computed states.
| { near: bottom-center; style.fill: "#D5F5E3"; style.stroke: "#229954" }
